The XinZhiZao reader follows the format description in OpenBoardView's
XZZPCBFile (credited there to @huertas, @inflex and @MuertoGB). DES itself
comes from the RustCrypto `des` crate (MIT/Apache-2.0).

The schematic viewer bundles PDF.js (pdfjs-dist), Copyright Mozilla
Foundation and contributors, licensed under the Apache License 2.0
(https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0). Its license and the licenses
of its bundled decoders ship in node_modules/pdfjs-dist and are copied into
the app under pdfjs/.

The reference values in src/knowledge/builtin.ts are read off measurement
pictures on Repair Wiki (https://repair.wiki; each page names its source), by
its contributors, licensed under Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 3.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/). The values in that file
are shared under the same license.

Text recognition for scanned schematics bundles Tesseract.js (tesseract.js,
tesseract.js-core; Copyright Jerome Wu and contributors) with the Tesseract
OCR engine (Copyright Google and contributors) and its English model
(@tesseract.js-data/eng, from tesseract-ocr/tessdata), all licensed under
the Apache License 2.0 (https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0). They
are copied into the app under ocr/.

Serial ports for multimeters are opened with the `serialport` crate
(MPL-2.0, https://github.com/serialport/serialport-rs).

The structured TVW reader is ported from EagleView's TeboBoard reader,
Copyright (c) 2019 Pavel Kovalenko, MIT licensed. The full notice is in
licenses/eagleview-MIT.txt.

Altium binary field layouts were checked against tscircuit/altium,
Copyright (c) 2026 tscircuit Inc., MIT licensed. Its notice is retained in
licenses/tscircuit-altium-MIT.txt.

The separate Allegro executable includes brd_parser by Yigit Berna,
revision f38fb8f48031eb78d654a78a79453e580b634f93, GPL-3.0.
It is executed locally through file IPC, not linked to the MIT library.
The complete corresponding source, Avero's modifications, license and
build instructions are in tools/allegro-reader and src-tauri/build.rs in
this repository and the GitHub source archive for the installed version:
https://github.com/meb99/Avero. The GPL license also ships with the app.

The ATE BV reader uses jetdb (MIT/Apache-2.0); compound Altium documents
use cfb (MIT). ODB++ and EasyEDA importers are original implementations
using the manufacturers' public interchange documentation.
